cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "AlcoLab: an open-source application for methanol screening by density and syringe-flow measurements"
abstract: >-
  AlcoLab is an open-source progressive web app for reagent-free semiquantitative
  screening of ethanol and methanol in hydroalcoholic mixtures, using a balance
  readable to 0.1 g and a 20 mL disposable syringe fitted with a 22-gauge needle.
  Composition is estimated by combining a density-based total alcohol mass fraction
  with the same-session sample-to-water syringe-flow ratio, compared against a
  literature-derived ternary viscosity grid (queried at a fixed 24 deg C layer) via
  a few-parameter empirical transfer model. This repository holds the application
  source code and the embedded scientific pipeline (Python/Pyodide). The editorial
  blog content of alcolab.org is maintained in a separate private repository and is
  not part of this archive.
